BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Rouge — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261122T180000
DTSTAMP:20261121T192054Z
UID:c585b763a184629bcbd6f48cff08@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Rouge is a sensuous and melancholy film about a beautiful ghos
 t searching for her lost lover in modern Hong Kong. Fleur (Anita Mui) and 
 “Twelfth Master” (Leslie Cheung) committed suicide fifty years ago\, i
 ntending to spend eternity together in Hell rather than be separated by hi
 s disapproving parents. But when “Twelfth Master” fails to join her in
  the afterlife\, Fleur returns to Earth to find him. She befriends a journ
 alist couple. Fascinated by her archaic clothes\, language\, and otherworl
 dly manner\, they agree to help. Slipping back and forth in time\, “ Rou
 ge is something like the Platonic ideal of a cinematic ghost story” (Den
 nis Lim\, Criterion Collection).\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https
 ://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331162-film-screening-rouge
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331162-film-screening-rouge
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Symphony Orchestra: The Nutcracker & Cinderella — Washi
 ngton\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261122T190000
DTSTAMP:20261121T192054Z
UID:df66f96954776d54f9ff3d9605b4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Be moved by two treasured fairy tales through the music of Tch
 aikovsky and Prokofiev\, conducted by Marie Jacquot in her NSO debut. Tcha
 ikovskys The Nutcracker Suite brings Clara\, the Sugar Plum Fairy\, and an
  enchanted Christmas Eve party to the concert stage\, while Prokofievs Cin
 derella Suite reimagines the timeless story with music that is playful and
  packed with clever turns. Between the ballets\, Jorge Federico Osorio cas
 ts a different kind of spell in Mozarts Piano Concerto No. 21\, famous for
  its slow\, haunting second movement. Three beloved works\, three worlds o
 f magic! There is a ticket limit of 8 tickets per person and per credit ca
 rd on this event.\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://cal
 endar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcracker-cinderella-
 5012
