SUMMARY:Are You For Sale? LIVE! with Miguel Gutierrez and Jane Raleigh —
  Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261211T130000
DTSTAMP:20261121T192054Z
UID:ff142e4ff5f89ad79a92934efa81@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a live taping of Season 2\, episode 2 of multi-dis
 ciplinary choreographer Miguel Gutierrez's podcast Are You For Sale? which
  examines the ethical entanglement between funding and dance-making. In th
 is free public conversation\, Miguel will talk to Jane Raleigh\, former Di
 rector of Dance Programming at the Kennedy Center\, about the current admi
 nistration’s political assault on cultural spaces. Together they will di
 scuss strategies for resistance and collectively ask\, how do we continue 
 to co-create nourishing art spaces? In the spirit of Are You For Sale? the
  conversation will be candid\, cathartic\, and community driven\, so bring
  your questions for this live recording.\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOrigin
 al listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/are-you-for-sale-live-with-migu
 el-gutierrez-and-jane-raleigh
