SUMMARY:A Winter in London — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261212T160000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261212T180000
DTSTAMP:20261121T192054Z
UID:ddc95e13a4bc1fd0927481993bf6@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A WINTER IN LONDON | PLACE & BELONGING Where do we belong? A p
 lace is more than a point on a map. It is its people\, traditions\, memori
 es\, movement\, sounds\, and stories. In A Winter in London\, our All Toge
 ther Now journey turns toward place and belonging. Through the musical lif
 e of London\, we explore how people give meaning to the places they inhabi
 t\, and how those places\, in turn\, become part of who they are. Together
  is where belonging begins: in the communities we inherit\, the communitie
 s we enter\, and the communities we help create. Program ・VAUGHAN WILLIA
 MS\, Folk Song Suite ・DVOŘÁK\, Romance for Violin and Orchestra – D.
 P. Reesman\, Violin ・DODSON\, What Child is This? ・DODSON\, Carol Sing
  \nCategory: Music\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-wint
 er-in-london/
LOCATION:St. Bartholomew&#8217\;s Episcopal Church\, 1790 LaVista Road NE
 \, Atlanta
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-winter-in-london/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
